# Infrastructure — agent capabilities

When `ark/.env` and `gh` are present, configure Gwenda infrastructure without asking the user to run Wrangler or `gh secret set` by hand. On a fresh nest: unlock Bitwarden (`bw-unlock`, or `export BW_SESSION=$(bw unlock --raw)`), run `npm run env:pull`, and `gh auth login` if needed. The env scripts persist `BW_SESSION` to `/commandhistory/.bw-session` in the devcontainer so later shells do not need a new unlock. Cloudflare and GitHub will not give secret values back.

This checkout often sits inside the **Gwenda nest** (`~/dev/gwenda`, or `/workspaces/gwenda` in a Codespace). Sibling `founders/`, `marketing/`, `operations/`, and `gwenda-mydrive/` are rclone FUSE mounts (workspace symlinks to `~/dev/mnt/gwenda/`). Nest `work/` is a flat local scratch pad for the file you are editing (export with `md-to-gdoc FILE.md remote:path` after confirmation). Shared Drive: `founders/`, `marketing/`, `operations/`. ClickUp keys may live in the nest `.env`, not `ark/.env`. Workspace map: nest `AGENTS.md`.

## Available credentials

| Source | What it provides |
|--------|------------------|
| Bitwarden (`bitwarden.eu`) | Source of truth for local secrets. Secure note `ark/.env.local` (Notes = dotenv). Pull with `npm run env:pull`. Optional `ark/.env.staging` / `ark/.env.production` for env backups. |
| `ark/.env` (gitignored) | `CLOUDFLARE_DEV_API_TOKEN` (local Pages, Wrangler; legacy alias `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`), `SANITY_API_TOKEN` (**Editor** robot `ark-local-editor`), `SANITY_PROJECT_ID=pn5yjro6`, deploy vars after `npm run setup:site-deploy`. Prefer `env:pull` / `setup:sanity-tokens` over hand-copying. |
| Nest `.env` (`~/dev/gwenda/.env` or `/workspaces/gwenda/.env`) | Workspace tools (e.g. ClickUp). Not a substitute for `ark/.env`. |
| `gh` CLI | When logged in as the repo owner: `repo` + `workflow`. Use `gh secret set`, `gh workflow run`, `gh variable list`. **Not always authenticated** in a new Codespace. |
| GitHub Actions secrets / Cloudflare Pages secrets | Set via `gh secret set` or `wrangler pages secret put`. **Never readable after write** (names only). |

Do **not** regenerate Cloudflare / Sanity / Baserow tokens on a fresh clone when Bitwarden already has them. Only run `setup:ci-secrets` / `setup:site-deploy` for first-time wiring or repair.

## Sanity tokens

- **Local Editor** (`ark-local-editor`) in `.env` — Studio, seeds, schema work. Cannot mint other tokens.
- **Mint/revoke** — personal `npx sanity login` (project Administrator), then `npm run setup:sanity-tokens`.
- **Deploy Studio** — GitHub `SANITY_DEPLOY_TOKEN` (`ark-ci-deploy-studio`).
- **Viewer** — GitHub `SANITY_API_TOKEN` (`ark-ci-viewer`) — site builds only.

Do not ask the user to create Sanity CI tokens manually; run `npm run setup:sanity-tokens` when needed.

## Site deploy (Studio → website rebuild)

Run **`npm run setup:site-deploy`** — it will:

1. Generate `DEPLOY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (or reuse from `.env`)
2. Set GitHub secrets (`DEPLOY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `DISPATCH_TOKEN` from `gh auth token`, `SANITY_STUDIO_SITE_DEPLOY_URL`)
3. Deploy `marketing/site-deploy-webhook` Worker and sync Worker secrets
4. Write `SANITY_STUDIO_SITE_DEPLOY_*` into repo-root `.env` for local Studio
5. Dispatch `studio.yml` to redeploy hosted Studio with deploy config

Local Studio (`npm run studio`) picks up deploy vars from `.env` via `scripts/with-env.mjs`. Hosted Studio gets them from GitHub secrets in `studio.yml`.

Do not ask the user to manually `gh secret set` deploy secrets or edit Worker URLs unless setup fails and needs diagnosis.

## Cloudflare

Use `CLOUDFLARE_DEV_API_TOKEN` from `.env` (legacy alias `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`) and `account_id` from `marketing/*/wrangler.toml` or `ops/*/wrangler.toml` for Worker deploys. GitHub CI still uses secret `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`. `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` is also in GitHub secrets for CI.

## After setup

- Restart local Studio if it was already running.
- Production hosted Studio: `npm run studio:deploy` (needs `SANITY_DEPLOY_TOKEN` in env or CI).
